#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Phase 460: CLAUDE.md: the log row; Book rules 11 and 13.
import sys, re
p = sys.argv[1]; s = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()
def rep(a, b):
    global s
    if s.count(a) != 1: raise SystemExit('found %d: %s' % (s.count(a), a[:60]))
    s = s.replace(a, b)
rep("PATH_STAGES order. Done: posture-hands, first-steps, note-names, staff, pulse (Level 1);", "PATH_STAGES order. Done: posture-hands, first-steps, note-names, staff, pulse, note-values (Level 1; note-values' guide page waits for her G1-G3);")
rep("Next: Level 1's note-values (draft v2, Phase 458, waiting for her answers to B4-B13 and G1-G3); then Level 2's time-signatures,", "Next: Level 2's time-signatures,")
rep("Note values: the breve, double dots.", "Note values: the breve, double dots (the drill's level 9 since Phase 460).")
ROW = """| 460 | 2026-10-13 | **Chapter 5, Notes & Rests, applied (her 20:57 '추천대로 가보자': B4-B13 as recommended).** patch460.py + nvbook460.jsx, nvapp460.jsx, nvwb460.jsx (in _workspace/chapter-review/g460/src). (1) Lesson Book, 7 pages, no draft marks: held beats' numbers lighter (B4, pages 3 and 4, each row counted), 'A dotted minim is a minim with a dot. It lasts three beats: the dot adds half the minim.' (B5), the coral sound line under every note (B6), no single quaver or quaver rest (B8), the dotted minim and the semibreve on one page (B13); 'A rest is a silence. It lasts a number of beats, like a note.'; the minim and semibreve rests half a space tall, sitting on line 3 and hanging from line 4; check 5 adds the semibreve rest. (2) On screen (B12): the book is the lesson; pages 2 to 6 each have a rhythm pad (the book's own tasks): listen, and each sound line grows while its note sounds; tap it, scored on the audio clock like chapter 3 (plRun, plMatch); the voice says 'and' between beats with quavers. (3) Drill (B10), 9 levels: name the note, how many beats, the matching rest, tap the rhythm, which count (an arrow on a note: 1, 1 +, 2 ...), rests (tap, then count the silence); then dotted crotchets and single quavers, semiquavers added up (Grades 1 and 2), the breve and double dots (Grade 4; AMEB Theory: single quavers Grade 1, semiquavers and dotted notes Grade 2; ABRSM: Grade 1, breve and double dots Grade 4). The tapped levels have no printed worksheet (a level can now say noPrint). (4) Workbook (B11): page 2 draw crotchets, how many beats, sound lines; 3 crotchet or minim, sound lines, count with held beats in grey boxes; 4 how many beats, sound lines, count; 5 walk or run-ning, write 1 + 2 +, notes from words; 6 note and rest, count every beat rests too, draw the rests; 7 the check-up (A-E, one per check). Teacher copy with every answer. (5) B9: rests on the staff, fix the bar, fill the bar and 'which bar did you hear?' moved to Time signatures, dotted notes, the dot lab and 'one beat = one apple' to Rhythm patterns (toolbox and the ends of both lessons); 'Count it out loud' counts 1 + 2 +; the tool category is 'Notes & rests'. Printables card: Chapter 5, the new Workbook page 4. A fresh reviewer's 19 points: all applied but one (the Korean picture captions 걷기 / 달리기 stay captions, as decided in Phase 457). Checks: fitall 128 paths 0 overflow; lbcheck 0/0 en and ko; wbcheck work, teacher, spread 0 overflow, check-up free 20 px; nv460qa (every level, 400 questions: answer offered, checks true, labels) 0 bad; nv460tap (pads and drill levels 4 and 6: right taps pass, an extra tap or quavers tapped as one fail); ws460, ll431/444 460, tn444, sf405, ch1app460 all pass. |
"""
m = re.search(r'^\| 459 \| [^\n]*\n', s, re.M)
if not m: raise SystemExit('row 459')
s = s[:m.end()] + ROW + s[m.end():]
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s); print('CLAUDE.md: log row 460, rules 11, 13')
